<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  V5.0.7020 — the Markets hero, at the render's actual values.

  Taken directly from project/Markets.dc.html rather than from memory:

    background: linear-gradient(155deg, rgba(16,60,52,.90), rgba(9,15,30,.97))
    border: 1px solid rgba(52,211,153,.36)

  Two things the app's other cards get wrong and this one does not:

  1. THE FILL IS TINTED TOWARD THE CARD'S OWN MEANING. This is the portfolio
     card, so it is green. The learning card in the same render is purple, the
     engine pills are purple/cyan/amber. Every card in the app currently shares
     one blue-grey fill, which is most of why the screens read as a list of
     identical boxes.

  2. ONE HAIRLINE, AT 36% ALPHA. The app's cards carry three concentric strokes
     (3dp at 0x24, 2dp at 0x4E, 1dp at 0xAD). A CSS box-shadow is a soft bloom;
     three stacked strokes is a hard ring, and stacking them on every surface is
     what turned every element into an outlined capsule.
-->
<shape xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android" android:shape="rectangle">
    <gradient android:type="linear" android:angle="295"
        android:startColor="#E6103C34" android:endColor="#F7090F1E"/>
    <stroke android:width="1dp" android:color="#5C34D399"/>
    <corners android:radius="24dp"/>
</shape>
